 We are building a social VR horror game about gorillas escaping a laboratory that experiments on animals. This document records the current game rules, Level 1, the proposed Listener level, the story, and the scene architecture so future work can build on the same decisions.
 
+## September 13 confirmed launch presentation direction
+
+**Confirmed design decision:** after reviewing the Option A prototype, Greg approved the **facility security-system boot** as the launch presentation direction for Runaway Chimps. The floating/abstract startup idea is no longer the selected alternative.
+
+**Confirmed travel correction:** successful Hub/level travel should be completely black, without a boot terminal, logo, tips or loading text. This supersedes older instructions below that describe visible Loading UI during travel; the Loading scene/lifecycle and full-stereo black coverage remain. Revisit an indicator only after measured transitions approach roughly **10 seconds**. That is a future design-review trigger, not a timer implemented here. Real travel failures still surface recovery/error feedback.
+
+**Implemented on `codex/security-boot-prototype`, draft PR #20, not merged:** a local scene-owned green/amber security terminal replaces cold-launch text/tips. Five indicators observe real Photon room membership, Hub load, rig alignment, avatar spawn and avatar visuals. Existing authentication, additive-load reuse, readiness, timeout and controller-trigger/desktop-R retry remain authoritative. The current branch also keeps `ACCESS GRANTED` readable for a short minimum dwell, forces the Loading canvas above partially loaded Hub UI, restores camera state on all presentation exits, and emits Editor/development milestone timing diagnostics. Travel builds no terminal/audio and suppresses legacy labels while retaining its existing rig/Photon/loading/fade/recovery lifecycle and XR overscan.
+
+**Planned separately / not implemented here:** native Quest/Meta system-splash configuration, final logo art, any surveillance-footage finish, CRT distortion, and final sound design. Greg's approval confirms the visual concept; it does not establish Unity/headset/Photon/Quest technical validation.
+
+**Validated source only:** Source integrity passed on the implemented prototype/polish revisions. **Pending validation:** Unity 2022.3.55f1 import/compile, normal startup, slow/failed connection and retry, interruption during fades, two-client Photon, both-eye headset coverage/readability, camera restoration, optional audio comfort and Quest performance. See [prototype setup and acceptance checks](security-boot-prototype.md). Source checks do not establish runtime success.
